WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.730
In 1992, the US state of New Jersey raised

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:09.290
its minimum wage from 4.25
to 5.05 dollars an hour.

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:13.260
Next door, Pennsylvania's
minimum wage did not change.

4
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.400
Two economists went to
count fast-food jobs on both

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.880
sides of the border.

6
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.600
So if a law lifts the lowest pay,

7
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.880
do some workers lose their jobs?

8
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.140
In this mission, you'll draw
the minimum wage diagram,

9
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.550
step by step.

10
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.810
Then you'll set the minimum
wage yourself in a graph lab,

11
00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.490
and watch what happens.

12
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:36.680
Your mission: find out what a
higher minimum wage does to jobs.
